{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":836,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ps.99","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Psalms 99","reference":"Psalms 99","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"Israel is required to praise God, for their hasty constitution both in church and state, ver."},{"verse":2,"text":"1-5."},{"verse":3,"text":"Some instances of the happy administration of it, ver."},{"verse":4,"text":"6-9."},{"verse":5,"text":"1.","scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":6,"text":"People - Such as are enemies to God and his people.","scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":7,"text":"Sitteth - Upon the ark.","scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":8,"text":"He is present with his people.","scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":9,"text":"Earth - The people of the earth.","scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":10,"text":"Moved - With fear and trembling.","scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":11,"text":"3.","scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":12,"text":"Them - All people.","scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":13,"text":"4.","scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":14,"text":"Judgment - Though his dominion be absolute, and his power irresistible, yet he manages it with righteousness.","scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":15,"text":"The king's strength is by a known Hebraism put for the strong, or powerful king.","scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":16,"text":"Equity - In all thy proceedings.","scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":17,"text":"5.","scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":18,"text":"Foot-stool - Before the ark, which is so called, 1 Chron. xxviii, 2.","scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":19,"text":"Holy - It is consecrated to be a pledge of God's presence.","scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":20,"text":"6.","scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":21,"text":"Moses - Moses before the institution of the priesthood executed that office, Exod. xxiv, 6.","scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":22,"text":"That call - Who used frequently and solemnly to intercede with God on the behalf of the people.","scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":23,"text":"7.","scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":24,"text":"Spake - To some of them: to Moses and Aaron, Exod. xix, 24; xxxiii, 9-11; 1 Sam. vii, 9, &c.","scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":25,"text":"8.","scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":26,"text":"Them - The intercessors before mentioned.","scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":27,"text":"Forgavest - The people for whom they prayed, so far as not to inflict that total destruction upon them which they deserved;","scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":99}}